  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let the equation of the plane be</p><p><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8757;</mo></math> it contains the point <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3,1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>&#8658;6</mtext><mo>&#8211;</mo><mtext>2</mtext><mo>+</mo><mtext>1</mtext><mo>&#8211;</mo><mtext>3</mtext><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br />Hence, the equation of the plane is<br /><math><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></msqrt><msqrt><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></math></p>"
  }
